    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHi,\r\n\r\nFirst, Thank you for the file plugin, coming from nvim-tree, this seems really more intuitive.\r\nOnly thing that I saw that would be missing is to copy the relative file path of the file currently highlighted in the file system using mini.files.\r\nI noticed that I often used this functionality with nvim-tree because it's quick to share to members of the team when working on team projects, that would be cool to have a mapping like `gY` to copy that.\r\nSo I would like to know first if that might be a functionnality that I can add as a plugin user in mini.file in the configuration? If so, how ?  \r\nIf not, does that align with the vision of mini.files to have this kind of feature? if that's the case I'm willing to contribute.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2023-11-13T20:45:10Z",
